# Build context filter for frontend/Dockerfile.
#
# Added with the release CI (.github/workflows) because this Dockerfile does
# `COPY . .` and there was no filter at all. Three separate reasons:
#
# 1. LEAK PREVENTION. `COPY . .` copies whatever is sitting in frontend/ into
#    a PUBLISHED image. A developer's stray `.env` would ship to a public
#    registry. .github/scripts/scan_image_secrets.py fails the build if that
#    ever happens; this file stops it happening.
#
# 2. CORRECTNESS. Without this, a HOST node_modules/ was copied over the
#    node_modules/ that `npm ci` had just installed in the image - i.e. the
#    Linux dependency tree got clobbered by whatever the developer's machine
#    (Windows, here) had built, including native binaries for the wrong
#    platform. `npm ci` runs before `COPY . .`, so excluding node_modules is
#    what makes that install actually count.
#
# 3. SPEED. The context went from hundreds of megabytes to a few.
#
# Everything `npm run build` (= `vite build`) needs is deliberately NOT
# excluded: index.html, src/, public/, vite.config.ts, svelte.config.js and
# the tsconfig*.json files all stay.

# Dependency tree - reinstalled in the image by `npm ci` (see reason 2).
node_modules

# Build and test output - regenerated by the image build, or irrelevant to it.
dist
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
.svelte-kit
.vite

# Test-only sources. The published image serves static assets; it does not
# run Playwright.
e2e
playwright.config.ts

# Credentials. Never in a build context, never in a published image.
.env
.env.*

# Docker's own files and local noise.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
npm-debug.log*
*.log
.DS_Store
